## Rules (these are checked by the review step)
1. The entry point is decorated with `@wrapper.entrypoint` and ends with `raise SystemExit(main())`.
2. Every per-item unit of work goes through `wrapper.run_item(item_id, fn, ...)` or `wrapper.log_item(...)` so item telemetry exists.
3. Never log secrets. Anything personal or confidential is passed with `sensitive=True` or `sensitive_keys=[...]`.
4. Untrusted text (scraped pages, documents) goes to `wrapper.llm_call(...)` ONLY in the `context=` argument, never inside `prompt=`; structured calls pass a `schema` and handle a `None` result explicitly.
5. Parameters come from `wrapper.param("name", default)`; honour `wrapper.is_dry_run()` before any side effect.
6. Credentials are the user's own session; never hard-code or read secrets from files.
7. Finish with `wrapper.set_result(...)` summarising counts.

## Worked example
Task: "Pull open invoices from System X and route each to the AP team".

Output:
```json
{"files": [
  {"path": "automation.yaml",
   "content": "name: automation-invoice-router\nversion: 0.1.0\nruntime: python\nentrypoint: main.py\nrequires: {wrapper_core: \">=0.1.0,<1.0.0\", execution_framework: \">=0.1.0,<1.0.0\"}\ntimeout_s: 1800\n"},
  {"path": "main.py",
   "content": "import wrapper_core as wrapper\n\n\ndef fetch_open_invoices(since):\n    \"\"\"Replace with the real System X call (prefer its API over the browser).\"\"\"\n    return []\n\n\ndef route(invoice):\n    if not invoice.get(\"vendor_id\"):\n        raise ValueError(\"missing required field: vendor_id\")  # DATA_ERROR -> item skipped, run continues\n    return \"AP\"\n\n\n@wrapper.entrypoint\ndef main():\n    since = wrapper.param(\"date_range\", \"yesterday\")\n    invoices = fetch_open_invoices(since)\n    wrapper.log_event(\"fetched\", {\"count\": len(invoices), \"since\": since})\n    routed = 0\n    for inv in invoices:\n        if wrapper.is_dry_run():\n            continue\n        if wrapper.run_item(inv[\"id\"], route, inv) is not None:\n            routed += 1\n    wrapper.set_result(fetched=len(invoices), routed=routed)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    raise SystemExit(main())\n"},
  {"path": "tests/test_main.py",
